{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e","id":693721,"title":"Blood Tenebrous 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-08T04:34:28-07:00","id":693721,"title":"Blood Tenebrous 2E","content":"Since <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> 2nd Edition came out, some of you may be wanting to get your vampires in on the fun. After all, other supernatural creatures can be part of the pack, now, too! Or maybe you just want some tools for opening up shadowy new horizons for your characters. Here you go! A couple of these (the fifth dot power in particular) might need a bit of tweaking, but I'll come back to it tomorrow. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Blood Tenebrous</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cOf all that is written, I love only what a person hath written with his blood. Write with blood, and thou wilt find that blood is spirit.&quot;</i><br /> \u2014 Friedrich Nietzsche</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Kine have long believed in spirits and shadowy realms unknown to vampires. Few among the Kindred can verify these beliefs; fewer still care. Why truck with hidden realms of spirits and magic when the blood runs hot in your doll's veins, the money flows through your accounts, and you wake up to face the Danse Macabre one more night? Leave such secrets buried and let the mortals ponder them. Vampires already raise more demons than they can put down.<br /> <br /> Some vampires seek out those secrets as hungrily as they do their next meal. They pursue occult mysteries and feed from them. In knowledge is power. In blood is life. Where the two overlap, vampiric blood magic flourishes. Brave or foolhardy vampires can learn to see and interact with the denizens of the spirit world. At the highest levels of power, they can even travel into the Shadow Realm, a bizarre world of spiritual, where Essence fills the body instead of blood.<br /> <br /> Even here, vampires are predators.<br /> <br /> The Discipline called Blood Tenebrous may have its origins in lost bloodlines or forgotten blood magic rites. Maybe it is the birthright of all Kindred. After all, shamanistic traditions and spirituality have existed for as long as the Kine themselves. Some see it as an inherent part of human consciousness, and vampires were once human. Should they not have that right? Is their own magic, fueled by stolen life, not evidence that they can work bloody miracles? If the mortals can master spirits and shamans can see into this shadowed realm, so too can the Kindred. As such, this Discipline can be treated as a bloodline Discipline, or a common Discipline requiring esoteric knowledge to develop, or an out-of-clan Discipline. Use whatever option best fits your chronicle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pulse of the Invisible (\u2022)</b></span><br /> Essence fuels the spirit world as blood fuels the world of flesh. The actions of living things creates it, and though they have not flesh like Kine, spirits are every bit as alive. With training, a vampire can hone her keen predatory senses to detect the flows of Essence. She can feel the presence of spiritual phenomena and track it like prey.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> This power is always active and requires no dice roll.<br /> Action: Instant (see below)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The vampire can feel whenever spiritual phenomena occurs in her immediate area (about a range of 5 times her Blood Potency in yards). If she possesses Auspex, add ten times her Auspex in yards to the range of this power. This spiritual sense tips her off to the presence of such powers, flooding her undead body with sensations she hasn't felt since the Embrace: goosebumps, a churning in her stomach, even the illusion of cold sweat. If she is heavily distracted, such as in combat or in the midst of feeding, the Storyteller can call for a perception roll.<br /> <br /> A vampire can focus her senses to see greater detail. With an instant action to focus (Storytellers might require a successful Wits + Occult roll to do so in combat), she can see spirits in Twilight, loci, verges, and similar spiritual phenomena until the end of the scene. She gains no ability to touch those things. While she can communicate with spirits in Twilight, she can only do so in the languages she knows, and not every spirit speaks mortal tongues. A vampire with this power qualifies to learn the Language (First Tongue) Merit if she desires, gaining the ability to fluently converse with spirits. For the duration of this effect, the vampire can also &quot;see&quot; the Fettered Condition as a glimmering aura enveloping the affected objects and people. If a spirit in Twilight state wishes to remain hidden (perhaps through the use of some power), it triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> With the expenditure of 1 Experience, the vampire also becomes capable of speaking the tongue of spirits. She can understand it and speak it as fluently as the spirits, though with a noticeable &quot;accent.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Blood is Life (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The power vampires gain from blood is something mystical, something they cannot fully explain. Blood represents life, and through this stolen life-force vampires sustain their unnatural immortality. Spirits are immortal, too, and yet very much alive, capable of growth. Vampires at this level of mastery learn how to feed from Essence and offer up their own in turn to sate spirit appetites.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> -<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Effect:</b> By spending a point of Willpower, the vampire may feed from a spirit like she would a living animal. This is not without risks. Many spirits are potent creatures and possess strange powers of their own, and this ability offers no additional protection. Feeding on spirits can be a dangerous proposition if the vampire has no leverage or considerable power of her own. The effect lasts for a single feeding. While risky, feeding from spirits does offer some advantages. Spirits are far more durable than mortals and can stand to lose much more Essence than humans can lose blood. Every 2 points of Essence grants 1 Vitae for these purposes. Each 2 points of Essence taken also causes one bashing damage to spirits, which are simply more durable than mortal creatures.<br /> <br /> The vampire can also spill some of her blood onto the ground, and allow it to rise as Essence for the consumption of hungry spirits. This costs 1 point of Willpower as well, and she simply spends however much Vitae she wishes to offer. Every point of Vitae translates to two points of Essence. This Essence lasts for about a minute, and carries a heavy resonance of both death and hunger.<br /> <br /> Note that using this power does not allow the vampire to feed on dematerialized spirits. Her eyes are bigger than her stomach, as the saying goes, unless she encounters a materialized spirit or finds herself in the Shadow Realm (perhaps by uses of higher levels of this Discipline).<br /> <br /> By spending 2 Experiences, the vampire can gain this ability as an innate ability. If she does so, it is considered always active and doesn't require Willpower to activate either facet of this power.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Under the Skin of the World (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Secrets lie hidden in the night. A world of supernatural predators lives just beneath human notice, preying upon them by night and vanishing during the day. Beyond a smothering veil called the Gauntlet, another world of predator and prey lies similarly hidden from the Kindred. Here, spirits of animals, plants, elemental forces, even concepts engage in the most ancient of life-and-death struggles. Secrets are buried throughout this spirit world, and there is power here, as well. Most vampires, even if they believed in the existence of a shadowy hidden realm of spirits, would not care. Blood is a mortal concern. Leave the spirits to their bizarre struggles, and let the Kindred remain to prey upon the Kine.<br /> <br /> Other vampires hunger for things besides blood. Secrets, powers, new realms to explore, and new advantages to exploit. What advantage might spirits and their world offer to a vampire's Danse Macabre? Few vampires bother with such things, and fewer still have any way to defend against it. Should a vampire plunge into the spirit world in search of occult mysteries and new powers, who knows what she might discover\u2014or become.<br /> <br /> This power allows a vampire to cross over into the spirit world, an act called Reaching. To them it feels like pushing through a thick canopy, or perhaps a semi-solid sheet of water, and emerging into a world where their dead skin feels alive once more. Vampires must Reach at a locus, a place where the two realms have been anchored to one another. Many loci are guarded, by werewolves or by greedy spirits on the other side, so a vampire who wishes to Reach across is well-served by investigating first. Of course, not all vampires have the luxury of time or choice. Even simply traveling to the spirit world is fraught with risks.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Realm is so called because it is a dark place, where the sun and moon are veiled. Night rules the spirit world, where the sky in most places remains dark enough that the vampire need not fear the sun. Nor does she suffer from the pull of daysleep, but she must continue to spend Vitae each day at approximately the same time she would rise at night. Despite this, it is easy to lose track of time as it would exist in the physical world. Unless the locus the vampire is using is hidden indoors, somewhere away from sunlight, Reaching back into the mortal world is very risky. The vampire might seek out the knowledge of a spirit to find out the time of day before crossing over.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Blood Tenebrous<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers:</b> Staring into reflective surface (+1), crossing into the Shadow during the day (-2), crossing into the Flesh during the day (+2)<br /> <br /> The transfer takes time: two turns per level of Gauntlet strength. See Werewolf: The Forsaken p. 101 for more information on the Gauntlet and Reaching. Spending a point of Vitae allows the vampire to disappear and reappear instantly on the other side.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The vampire fails to pierce the Gauntlet and comes away \u201ctarred\u201d in ephemeral gunk. She may not attempt to Reach again for one full day.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The character fails to cross over into the other world. She may try again in the same scene, but it requires a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The character vanishes from her current world and passes through the Gauntlet. She reappears in her destination realm a short time later.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The vampire slips from one world to the other as easily as she might open a door and walk through. She transfers instantly and may act as normal on her very next turn.<br /> <br /> If the vampire spends 3 Experiences, she can gain this ability as an inherent power, removing the Willpower cost. She can spend an additional 2 Experiences after doing so to learn how to bring others across. This functions the same way as traveling by herself, although each additional traveler levies a -1 penalty on the roll. Unconscious travelers instead impose a -2 penalty, and actively unwilling travelers a -4 penalty. This requires a greater exertion of the vampire's shadowy blood magic. Additional passengers cost 1 Vitae each.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pangaean Predator (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> Legends speak of a hunter's paradise long ago vanished from the world. Mortals and spirits alike hunted this strange border realm, or crossed through it to reach worlds not their own. The primeval natives of this realm long ago went extinct when their world disappeared, but the vampire has inherited their legacy as hunter of both flesh and spirit. To the Shadow Realm she is no longer an outsider, but now a full participant in the bloody struggle to survive\u2014for better or worse. Spirits begrudge her place in the food chain just as they would their own kind, and gain a healthy respect for the vampire's ability as a predator.<br /> <br /> The vampire gains an &quot;honorary&quot; spirit Rank equal to her dots in this Discipline or her Blood Potency, whichever is lower. This affords her incidental bonuses to intimidation or persuasion among lesser spirits, and lets her unarmed attacks act as banes against spirits two or more Ranks lower. Powerful Shadow-Kindred become quite capable of tearing weaker spirits to shreds and hold their own against the stronger ones, earning their place in the ephemeral ecosystem. Note that this ability only counts toward the vampire <i>against </i>spirits, and not the reverse. This gives them an advantage against these bizarre entities, one which most vampires are quick to exploit.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Umbral Chrysalis (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> At the pinnacle of her spiritual power a vampire undergoes something of a transformation. She retreats to a dark, sunless place in the Shadow and buries herself in the earth. For a number of days equal to her Blood Potency she remains so buried, as if in torpor, without needing to spend Vitae. Blood bubbles up to soak the earth where she rests, but most spirits dare not try to devour its Essence. They sense the predator lurking beneath, the great changes taking place, the danger to rise from shadowed grave-dirt and take on new form. After the time has passed, the vampire emerges from her spirit-grave transformed into a more effective Shadow-stalking predator.<br /> <br /> This power is permanent and requires no roll. When the vampire first learns this Discipline, she chooses one of the options below. She may spend Experiences afterward to gain the powers she didn't originally choose (as though buying this level over again), or if she has enough Experiences saved up, may spend them to gain all the powers during the first chrysalis. These powers come at something of a cost, limiting the vampire's maximum Humanity by 1 per power. As she becomes more spirit-like and alien, it becomes harder to remember what Humanity truly means.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The vampire may exchange one of her banes for a bane appropriate to a spirit equal to her honorary Rank. She may not choose fire or sunlight to change this way, but may substitute clan banes, personal banes gained from eroding Humanity, or even staking the heart. She can only choose one such bane to exchange this way.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Spirits can increase their abilities through Essence, and the vampire has learned how to replicate some of that power. When she spends Vitae on physical intensity, she may choose to have the bonus persist until the end of the scene. If she does, the total bonus is limited to her honorary spirit Rank + 2. She cannot spend more Vitae to increase the chosen Physical Attribute bonus, even if her allowed Vitae per turn would let her boost the dice pool beyond (Rank + 2) additional dice. Her Essence-charged Vitae can sustain heightened physical abilities for longer than normal Vitae, but at the cost of sheer depth of power. While this power is active, she suffers a penalty on detachment rolls and rolls to resist frenzy equal to her honorary Rank. Her Beast is riled and flush with power, her Humanity's voice drowned out by the wanton urges that spirits feel.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The vampire gains dots in Influence equal to her honorary spirit Rank. The chosen Influence must be appropriate to the vampire's character and other powers. Influence (Blood) or Influence (Darkness) are common types of Influence gained this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 10-08-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T05:36:52-07:00","id":693778,"title":"","content":"I have two questions and an observation:<br /> <br /> First, is the one experience you can sped for the first dot in order to converse with spirits simply mean purchasing the first tongue merit, or does that only allow understanding and you need both for two-way communication?<br /> <br /> Second, if you opt for the second option of the five dot power, do you still need to spend 1 vitae per 2 attribute dots, or do you only get 1 per vitae? If the former, what happens if the vampire has an odd spirit rank? Do they get the extra die for one turn only or does it just fizzle? <br /> <br /> Observation: Said power appears to be more effective the lower a vampire's blood potency is. At 1 dot, the cap is 3 bonus dice, which is more than physical intensity can bestow at that level. at 2 dots they are equal, and it's only at 3 dots or above that the limit becomes a drawback. This drawback starts small, and gets bigger the higher you go, quickly becoming huge as you rise past blood potency 6. Is all this intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T06:30:02-07:00","id":693811,"title":"","content":"Great job, really complete. I like specially the description of the 5th dot. Very evocative. I have two sugestions to your work: <br /> <br /> - The name of the Second Point, <b>&quot;Blood is Life&quot;</b>... how do you like it as <b>&quot;Blood's Essence&quot;</b>? <br /> <br /> - About the Fifth Point, <b>&quot;Umbra Chrysalis&quot;</b>. Maybe a nice adition to it would be having as many &quot;upgrades&quot; as points has the vampire in the Discipline? These extra evolutions could be unlocked adding spiritual Numina, taken from whatever Spirits had consumed the vampire (ala <b>&quot;Beast Skin&quot;</b>, Protean 3). If you want to keep the challenge, and not letting the vampire go easily hunting for low rank Spirits, it could have a restriction on the Spirit Rank being at least the same as the vampire's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:05:39-07:00","id":693982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693778#post693778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, if you opt for the second option of the five dot power, do you still need to spend 1 vitae per 2 attribute dots, or do you only get 1 per vitae? If the former, what happens if the vampire has an odd spirit rank? Do they get the extra die for one turn only or does it just fizzle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing that Spirits spend 1 Essence to increase one of their Attributes by one, and one Vitae is worth 2 Essence, I guess it is still 2 bonus dice per Vitae for a Vampire. I guess the last die would fizzle, if the vampire has an odd spirit rank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693778#post693778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observation: Said power appears to be more effective the lower a vampire's blood potency is. At 1 dot, the cap is 3 bonus dice, which is more than physical intensity can bestow at that level. at 2 dots they are equal, and it's only at 3 dots or above that the limit becomes a drawback. This drawback starts small, and gets bigger the higher you go, quickly becoming huge as you rise past blood potency 6. Is all this intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>This problem could easily be solved by allowing the Vampire to still use Physical Intensity while Spiritual Intensity is active, but always using the highest bonus of both (the bonusses do not stack). That way a high Blood Potency vampire can still reach high bonusses.<br /> <br /> If this change were to be implemented, I would have activating Spiritual Intensity cost an Instant action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693811#post693811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name of the Second Point, <b>&quot;Blood is Life&quot;</b>... how do you like it as <b>&quot;Blood's Essence&quot;</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like &quot;Blood is Life&quot; for nostalgic reasons. The first three powers have names identical to those of the original Blood Tenebrous Discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693811#post693811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Fifth Point, <b>&quot;Umbra Chrysalis&quot;</b>. Maybe a nice adition to it would be having as many &quot;upgrades&quot; as points has the vampire in the Discipline? These extra evolutions could be unlocked adding spiritual Numina, taken from whatever Spirits had consumed the vampire (ala <b>&quot;Beast Skin&quot;</b>, Protean 3). If you want to keep the challenge, and not letting the vampire go easily hunting for low rank Spirits, it could have a restriction on the Spirit Rank being at least the same as the vampire's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, making the number of upgrades depend on the amount of points in the Discipline does not really make sense as a mechanic here, as when one reaches this power, that will always be five.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I wouldn't allow the Vampire to take Numen, as they aren't exactly balanced for player use. Instead, I would allow the vampire to learn Numina like powers as Blood Tenebrous 5 Devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T15:06:52-07:00","id":694227,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the comments, y'all. This is why I enjoy bringing stuff to the forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693778#post693778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, is the one experience you can sped for the first dot in order to converse with spirits simply mean purchasing the first tongue merit, or does that only allow understanding and you need both for two-way communication?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically just purchasing the Language (First Tongue) Merit. You can understand and converse in the First Tongue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=693778#post693778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, if you opt for the second option of the five dot power, do you still need to spend 1 vitae per 2 attribute dots, or do you only get 1 per vitae? If the former, what happens if the vampire has an odd spirit rank? Do they get the extra die for one turn only or does it just fizzle?<br /> <br /> Observation: Said power appears to be more effective the lower a vampire's blood potency is. At 1 dot, the cap is 3 bonus dice, which is more than physical intensity can bestow at that level. at 2 dots they are equal, and it's only at 3 dots or above that the limit becomes a drawback. This drawback starts small, and gets bigger the higher you go, quickly becoming huge as you rise past blood potency 6. Is all this intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was intentional, but it might need some revision. The idea was that the vampire couldn't do a scene-long buff with Vitae, then spend the normal amount on physical intensity to go to really ridiculous levels. I suppose one could simply say you can blood buff as normal except make it last for the scene; maybe if you do it that way, it's 1 Vitae per +1, instead of 1 for +2. I didn't want it to be <i>too </i>powerful, but it's also the ultimate power of the Discipline, so it should be strong.<br /> <br /> I considered other options, like allowing vampires to learn Numina, but didn't for the reasons Penta mentioned. They're not really designed for player use. Just possessing the Discipline at all, especially at mastery, is grounds enough to develop Devotions based on Numina and such.<br /> <br /> Another option I considered was letting vampires heal naturally and not have to spend Vitae to remain awake\u2014but only while in the Shadow. The fluff being that they're subconsciously &quot;feeding&quot; on ambient Essence, like spirits do when near Conditions that relate to them (like Resonant Conditions).<br /> <br /> I also considered stuff like bloody discorporation and a few other spirit-like things. Kind of fun to see behind the scenes, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:51:50-07:00","id":694320,"title":"","content":"Doesn't one dot in the Unnatural Affinity Merit give the ability to take Vitae from materialized spirits? If so, the only new benefit from Blood is Life is the power to turn Vitae into Essence - and that isn't worth spending a Willpower point for. I'd make Blood is Life costless in both directions, apart from the Vitae lost to a spirit of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T17:20:23-07:00","id":694375,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure you have to be able to feed from spirits before Unnatural Affinity works. Unnatural affinity would only make Spirits equivalent to vitae, not grant the ability to feed from spirits. Unnatural Affinity is mainly for high blood potency vampires with vitae only feeding restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T23:13:03-07:00","id":694588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=694375#post694375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure you have to be able to feed from spirits before Unnatural Affinity works. Unnatural affinity would only make Spirits equivalent to vitae, not grant the ability to feed from spirits. Unnatural Affinity is mainly for high blood potency vampires with vitae only feeding restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div> According to the book of spirits, vampires don't need a special ability to feed on some spirits, if the spirit looks like something that would have blood, it's edible. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T23:56:47-07:00","id":694602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=694375#post694375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure you have to be able to feed from spirits before Unnatural Affinity works. Unnatural affinity would only make Spirits equivalent to vitae, not grant the ability to feed from spirits. Unnatural Affinity is mainly for high blood potency vampires with vitae only feeding restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also in the camp of people who say that Vampires can feed on supernaturals with blood just fine, but that Unnatural Affinity only lets you treat supernatural blood as Vitae for feeding restrictions. But I remember from earlier discussions that some people believe that you need this Merit to feed on supernaturals at all.<br /> <br /> The Merit calls out that the ST should work with the player to find a way in which the Vampire can feed in the supernatural. As StSword noted, according to book of Spirits, vampires can feed on spirits who look like something that would have blood. So Blood of Life still provides the extra option to feed on spirits that are not animal or human like, such as artificial, elemental and some conceptual spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=694320#post694320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't one dot in the Unnatural Affinity Merit give the ability to take Vitae from materialized spirits? If so, the only new benefit from Blood is Life is the power to turn Vitae into Essence - and that isn't worth spending a Willpower point for. I'd make Blood is Life costless in both directions, apart from the Vitae lost to a spirit of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we disregard that Blood is Life is necessary to feed from some spirits, I think you are underestimating the worth of being able to turn Vitae into Essence. Without this ability it is impossible to negotiate with spirits, and being able to turn Vitae into Essence at a 1:2 ratio makes you even better at bribing spirits than werewolves are, even if it is restricted to spirits of death and darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:51:59-07:00","id":694642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=694602#post694602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we disregard that Blood is Life is necessary to feed from some spirits, I think you are underestimating the worth of being able to turn Vitae into Essence. Without this ability it is impossible to negotiate with spirits, and being able to turn Vitae into Essence at a 1:2 ratio makes you even better at bribing spirits than werewolves are, even if it is restricted to spirits of death and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't go so far as to say it's impossible to make deals with spirits without the ability to turn blood into vitae.<br /> <br /> It certainly makes it a lot easier, but a vampire could still tempt say a fire spirit with the promise to burn a building or two, if the favor asked is proportionate. <br /> <br /> Heck, in dark eras, the new vampire covenant's special ability is a favor network with supernaturals, which includes thing as common place as other gameline protagonists up to saints or cosmic principles such as say Winter or Death ala Changeling. <br /> <br /> So there's no reason to believe that those vampires couldn't have favors- fire spirits or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:22:05-07:00","id":694884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=694642#post694642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go so far as to say it's impossible to make deals with spirits without the ability to turn blood into vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you are correct. I misremembered the rules for Social Maneuvering spirits a little bit. Spirits <i>have</i> to be paid as otherwise they cannot agree to deals. But while that payment is often at least two Essence points, it can also be removing a spirit from politics or changing the material world to provide some appropriate Essence.<br /> <br /> But the power thus still enables the Vampire to negotiate with spirits, without first having to go on quests to just have the spirit hear him out. It removes an extra hurdle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:27:04-07:00","id":854341,"title":"","content":"After the 1e version came out, I basically had an ancient master allow herself to be possessed by a major spirit for a little deus ex machina. In order to keep that in the NPC's arsenal, should I make that an additional possibility for the Umbral Chrysalis, or should I call it a devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T00:23:48-07:00","id":854379,"title":"","content":"I'd stick with a Devotion, which gives the best of both worlds, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:43:40-07:00","id":854548,"title":"","content":"So, I may be a little overcritical simply because I've done my own version of 2e Blood Tenebrous, but regardless:<ul><li>The second level, as written, seems to be a disadvantage for feeding on spirits. I know there's nothing explicitly saying it by default in 2e, but previously Vampires could feed on spirits as if they had vampire-like blood, though risked taking on some shadow sickness-like effects. At the very least, as has been mentioned, Unnatural Affinity would allow it with the same restriction of needing to be able to actually physically feed. You might want to change it to instead say they can simply feed safely and allow it to work on Twilight form spirits. And either way, 1 Willpower per use for either effect also seems excessively expensive by 2e standards.</li> <li>I'm not sure how I feel about the powers that let you spend additional Experiences to build upon the Discipline. That seems like something you'd just create as a Devotion for some of them (Bringing others across the Gauntlet, kinda like how Obfuscate has Cloak the Gathering). Or in the case of level 1, the simple mention of being able to buy the Language merit seems like enough.</li> <li>Overall this doesn't seem to capture the feel most 2e disciplines have of building upon each other.</li> <li>That said, I do really like what you've done for the 4th and 5th levels.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-28-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:22:06-07:00","id":854661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854548#post854548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I may be a little overcritical simply because I've done my own version of 2e Blood Tenebrous, but regardless:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in seeing that one!<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=falco1029;n854548]The second level, as written, seems to be a disadvantage for feeding on spirits. I know there's nothing explicitly saying it by default in 2e, but previously Vampires could feed on spirits as if they had vampire-like blood, though risked taking on some shadow sickness-like effects. At the very least, as has been mentioned, Unnatural Affinity would allow it with the same restriction of needing to be able to actually physically feed. You might want to change it to instead say they can simply feed safely and allow it to work on Twilight form spirits. And either way, 1 Willpower per use for either effect also seems excessively expensive by 2e standards.[/quote[<br /> <br /> I think now you'd need Unnatural Affinity, as you can't inherently feed on other creatures for proper sustenance. I like the idea of them being able to feed on Twilight form spirits. Maybe it could allow them to &quot;feed&quot; on locus Essence, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854548#post854548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about the powers that let you spend additional Experiences to build upon the Discipline. That seems like something you'd just create as a Devotion for some of them (Bringing others across the Gauntlet, kinda like how Obfuscate has Cloak the Gathering). Or in the case of level 1, the simple mention of being able to buy the Language merit seems like enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, Protean (and, I think, some others) allowed you to do that. Checking now, there doesn't seem to be any mention of it in 2E, so maybe I'll rewrite it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854548#post854548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall this doesn't seem to capture the feel most 2e disciplines have of building upon each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It progresses from sensing spirits and communicating with them, to being able to feed on them (though I may change that up a bit), travel into the Shadow Realm, gain an honorary spirit Rank, and finally transform your body to gain some of the benefits of spirits. The individual implementations might need some work, but it seems like there's at least a sense of progression to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854548#post854548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I do really like what you've done for the 4th and 5th levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I wasn't sure about the 5th-level, but most everyone seems to like it as is, so that works for me. Considering I would like to play a vampire in a crossover game sometime, this Discipline would certainly make being part of a pack a lot easier!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:38:19-07:00","id":854676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854661#post854661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be interested in seeing that one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nmvnt1UlBBR3DI6_Z1gFyqvPbSQtYi1pp6yIrcowHYM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yIrcowHYM/edit</a><br /> You can feel free to pick it apart in turn but I wouldnt wanna hijack your thread XD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think now you'd need Unnatural Affinity, as you can't inherently feed on other creatures for proper sustenance. I like the idea of them being able to feed on Twilight form spirits. Maybe it could allow them to &quot;feed&quot; on locus Essence, too. </div> </div> </div>I always figured that Unnatural Affinity was an elder thing; you only need it if you can't feed on 'humans' anymore, or otherwise have some weakness that prevents it. But yeah, that does sound good, though be careful about allowing them to get too much from a locus; i'd limit it to maybe once per week so a Vampire can't just hang out at a Loci and never need to feed (I ran into a similar problem when I remade fontal rituals).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1E, Protean (and, I think, some others) allowed you to do that. Checking now, there doesn't seem to be any mention of it in 2E, so maybe I'll rewrite it. </div> </div> </div>Right. I mean, nothing explicitly prevents it, and don't get me wrong, I don't mind the 'buy the power again' thing you have at the 5th level, I just think it ends up looking messy to add 'Add 1xp extra cost do do X and Y, or 2 for Z'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It progresses from sensing spirits and communicating with them, to being able to feed on them (though I may change that up a bit), travel into the Shadow Realm, gain an honorary spirit Rank, and finally transform your body to gain some of the benefits of spirits. The individual implementations might need some work, but it seems like there's at least a sense of progression to me. </div> </div> </div> I may have misstated my point; I see the natural progression, but the powers don't really interact with each other at all is all I meant. Dominate's higher levels use Mesmerized, for instance, and Obfuscate 2 lets you use other levels on others, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks! I wasn't sure about the 5th-level, but most everyone seems to like it as is, so that works for me. Considering I would like to play a vampire in a crossover game sometime, this Discipline would certainly make being part of a pack a lot easier! </div> </div> </div>Heh I'm the same way about liking to make stuff that facilitates crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-28-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:50:26-07:00","id":854703,"title":"","content":"Alrighty! Let's take a crack at revising this one, shall we? I'll cut out a lot of the fluff text, just looking at rules here for the moment. I considered letting vampires play with Conditions and Manifestations, but I'm not sure how that would work thematically or mechanically. Mostly, I wanted to tighten up the rules here.<br /> <br /> This Discipline has a prerequisite of Unnatural Affinity (Spirits).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pulse of the Invisible (\u2022)</b></span><br /> Essence fuels the spirit world as blood fuels the world of flesh. The actions of living things creates it, and though they have not flesh like Kine, spirits are every bit as alive. With training, a vampire can hone her keen predatory senses to detect the flows of Essence. She can feel the presence of spiritual phenomena and track it like prey.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> This power is always active and requires no dice roll.<br /> Action: Instant (see below)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The vampire can feel whenever spiritual phenomena occurs within Short Range. If she possesses Auspex, increase the range to Medium. This spiritual sense tips her off to the presence of such powers, flooding her undead body with sensations she hasn't felt since the Embrace: goosebumps, a churning in her stomach, even the illusion of cold sweat. If she is heavily distracted, such as in combat or in the midst of feeding, the Storyteller can call for a perception roll.<br /> <br /> A vampire can focus her senses to see greater detail. With an instant action to focus (Storytellers might require a successful Wits + Occult roll to do so in combat), she can see spirits in Twilight, loci, verges, and similar spiritual phenomena until the end of the scene. She gains no ability to touch those things. While she can communicate with spirits in Twilight, she can only do so in the languages she knows, and not every spirit speaks mortal tongues. A vampire with this power qualifies to learn the Language (First Tongue) Merit if she desires, gaining the ability to fluently converse with spirits. For the duration of this effect, the vampire can also &quot;see&quot; the Fettered Condition as a glimmering aura enveloping the affected objects and people. If a spirit in Twilight state wishes to remain hidden (perhaps through the use of some power), it triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Blood is Life (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The power vampires gain from blood is something mystical, something they cannot fully explain. Blood represents life, and through this stolen life-force vampires sustain their unnatural immortality. Spirits are immortal, too, and yet very much alive, capable of growth. Vampires at this level of mastery learn how to feed from Essence and offer up their own in turn to sate spirit appetites.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> -<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Effect:</b> A vampire with this power may feed on spirits in Twilight. She immerses herself in the spirit's incorporeal form and &quot;breathes&quot; in the life essence. This is not without risks. Many spirits are potent creatures with strange powers of their own, and this ability offers no additional protection. While risky, feeding from spirits does offer some advantages. Spirits are far more durable than mortals and can stand to lose much more Essence than humans can lose blood. Every 2 points of Essence grants 1 Vitae for these purposes. Each 2 points of Essence taken also causes one bashing damage to spirits, which are simply more durable than mortal creatures.<br /> <br /> The vampire can also spill some of her blood onto the ground, and allow it to rise as Essence for the consumption of hungry spirits. She simply spends however much Vitae she wishes to offer. Every point of Vitae translates to two points of Essence. This Essence lasts for about a minute, and carries a heavy resonance of both death and hunger. The Essence consumed this way carries with it the possibility of blood bonds as well as Vitae addiction.<br /> <br /> Finally, this power allows vampires to feed on Essence generated by loci. The character must touch or symbolically interact with the locus and spend one turn per point of Essence consumed. Each point translates to 1 Vitae. The vampire may only draw a number of Vitae equal to her Blood Potency per day.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Under the Skin of the World (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Secrets lie hidden in the night. A world of supernatural predators lives just beneath human notice, preying upon them by night and vanishing during the day. Beyond a smothering veil called the Gauntlet, another world of predator and prey lies similarly hidden from the Kindred. Here, spirits of animals, plants, elemental forces, even concepts engage in the most ancient of life-and-death struggles. Secrets are buried throughout this spirit world, and there is power here, as well. Most vampires, even if they believed in the existence of a shadowy hidden realm of spirits, would not care. Blood is a mortal concern. Leave the spirits to their bizarre struggles, and let the Kindred remain to prey upon the Kine.<br /> <br /> Other vampires hunger for things besides blood. Secrets, powers, new realms to explore, and new advantages to exploit. What advantage might spirits and their world offer to a vampire's Danse Macabre? Few vampires bother with such things, and fewer still have any way to defend against it. Should a vampire plunge into the spirit world in search of occult mysteries and new powers, who knows what she might discover\u2014or become.<br /> <br /> This power allows a vampire to cross over into the spirit world, an act called Reaching. To them it feels like pushing through a thick canopy, or perhaps a semi-solid sheet of water, and emerging into a world where their dead skin feels alive once more. Vampires must Reach at a locus, a place where the two realms have been anchored to one another. Many loci are guarded, by werewolves or by greedy spirits on the other side, so a vampire who wishes to Reach across is well-served by investigating first. Of course, not all vampires have the luxury of time or choice. Even simply traveling to the spirit world is fraught with risks.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Realm is so called because it is a dark place, where the sun and moon are veiled. Night rules the spirit world, where the sky in most places remains dark enough that the vampire need not fear the sun. Nor does she suffer from the pull of daysleep, but she must continue to spend Vitae each day at approximately the same time she would rise at night. Despite this, it is easy to lose track of time as it would exist in the physical world. Unless the locus the vampire is using is hidden indoors, somewhere away from sunlight, Reaching back into the mortal world is very risky. The vampire might seek out the knowledge of a spirit to find out the time of day before crossing over.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Blood Tenebrous<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers:</b> Staring into reflective surface (+1), crossing into the Shadow during the day (-4), crossing into the Flesh during the day (-2)<br /> <br /> The transfer takes time: two turns per level of Gauntlet strength. See <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken p. 101</b> for more information on the Gauntlet and Reaching. Spending a point of Vitae allows the vampire to disappear and reappear instantly on the other side. The vampire may attempt to bring others across with her. Each additional traveler levies a -1 penalty on the roll. Unconscious travelers instead impose a -2 penalty, and actively unwilling travelers a -4 penalty. This requires a greater exertion. Additional passengers cost 1 Vitae each.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The vampire fails to pierce the Gauntlet and comes away \u201ctarred\u201d in ephemeral gunk. She may not attempt to Reach again for one full day.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The character fails to cross over into the other world. She may try again in the same scene, but it requires a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The character vanishes from her current world and passes through the Gauntlet. She reappears in her destination realm a short time later.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The vampire slips from one world to the other as easily as she might open a door and walk through. She transfers instantly and may act as normal on her very next turn.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pangaean Predator (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> Legends speak of a hunter's paradise long ago vanished from the world. Mortals and spirits alike hunted this strange border realm, or crossed through it to reach worlds not their own. The primeval natives of this realm long ago went extinct when their world disappeared, but the vampire has inherited their legacy as hunter of both flesh and spirit. To the Shadow Realm she is no longer an outsider, but now a full participant in the bloody struggle to survive\u2014for better or worse. Spirits begrudge her place in the food chain just as they would their own kind, and gain a healthy respect for the vampire's ability as a predator.<br /> <br /> The vampire gains an &quot;honorary&quot; spirit Rank equal to her dots in this Discipline or her Blood Potency, whichever is lower. This affords her incidental bonuses to intimidation or persuasion among lesser spirits, and lets her unarmed attacks act as banes against spirits two or more Ranks lower. Powerful Shadow-Kindred become quite capable of tearing weaker spirits to shreds and hold their own against the stronger ones, earning their place in the ephemeral ecosystem. Note that this ability only counts toward the vampire <i>against </i>spirits, and not the reverse. This gives them an advantage against these bizarre entities, one which most vampires are quick to exploit.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Umbral Chrysalis (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> At the pinnacle of her spiritual power a vampire undergoes something of a transformation. She retreats to a dark, sunless place in the Shadow and buries herself in the earth. For a number of days equal to her Blood Potency she remains so buried, as if in torpor, without needing to spend Vitae. Blood bubbles up to soak the earth where she rests, but most spirits dare not try to devour its Essence. They sense the predator lurking beneath, the great changes taking place, the danger to rise from shadowed grave-dirt and take on new form. After the time has passed, the vampire emerges from her spirit-grave transformed into a more effective Shadow-stalking predator.<br /> <br /> This power is permanent and requires no roll. When the vampire first learns this Discipline, she chooses one of the options below. She may spend Experiences afterward to gain the powers she didn't originally choose (as though buying this level over again), or if she has enough Experiences saved up, may spend them to gain all the powers during the first chrysalis. These powers come at something of a cost, limiting the vampire's maximum Humanity by 1 per power. As she becomes more spirit-like and alien, it becomes harder to remember what Humanity truly means.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The vampire may exchange one of her banes for a bane appropriate to a spirit equal to her honorary Rank. She may not choose fire or sunlight to change this way, but may substitute clan banes, personal banes gained from eroding Humanity, or even staking the heart. She can only choose one such bane to exchange this way.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Spirits can increase their abilities through Essence, and the vampire has learned how to replicate some of that power. When she spends Vitae on physical intensity, she may choose to have the bonus persist until the end of the scene. If she does, the total bonus is limited to her honorary spirit Rank + 2. She cannot spend more Vitae to increase the chosen Physical Attribute bonus, even if her allowed Vitae per turn would let her boost the dice pool beyond (Rank + 2) additional dice. Her Essence-charged Vitae can sustain heightened physical abilities for longer than normal Vitae, but at the cost of sheer depth of power. While this power is active, she suffers a penalty on detachment rolls and rolls to resist frenzy equal to her honorary Rank. Her Beast is riled and flush with power, her Humanity's voice drowned out by the wanton urges that spirits feel.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The vampire gains dots in Influence equal to her honorary spirit Rank. The chosen Influence must be appropriate to the vampire's character and other powers. Influence (Blood) or Influence (Darkness) are common types of Influence gained this way.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:21:43-07:00","id":854853,"title":"","content":"The changes seem to take care of any issues I had noticed, though I don't know why Vitae to Essence is a 1 to 2 ratio?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T21:05:30-07:00","id":854862,"title":"","content":"Mostly because Essence seems to be easier to come by in large quantities. I suppose it doesn't break anything to have it be 1:1, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T10:01:13-07:00","id":855121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/693721-blood-tenebrous-2e?p=854862#post854862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because Essence seems to be easier to come by in large quantities. I suppose it doesn't break anything to have it be 1:1, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've always seen it as comparable for an individual spirit; it causes problems for them if they feed on essence of a different type (mainly, it leads them towards becoming hated magaths), and I think the combination of loci not being hugely plentiful combined with specific resonances of essence being potentially rare, it about comes out to a spirit having the same difficulties to feeding as a Vampire.<br /> <br /> I did also want to mention, looking it over again, I think allowing BP essence per day from a loci is a bit much. I think per week makes more sense because that lines up with the Herd merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:22:57-07:00","id":855515,"title":"","content":"Hey Claire sense Dark Eras has come out do you got any plans to implement some things from Pangaean in Neolithic era?<br /> After all your goal so far seems to make the vampire into a hunter of both Flesh and Spirit.<br /> <br /> Never mind Pangaean have access to Arcane but other then that they are nearly identical to spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":".  I have Read Pangaean. 04-01-2016, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}